# Share URI ↔ local map (Cursor)

On Cursor IDE and cursor-sdk hosts that mount the ULG shares, resolve Share URIs to local paths when direct file tools are cheaper. Mounts may change; **durable prose cites Share URIs only**.

| Share | Local mount (Cursor / cursor_sdk) |
|---|---|
| `cortex://` | `/mnt/torus/mcp-data/files/` |
| `workspaces://` | `/mnt/torus/projects/` |

Examples: `cortex://notes/system/specs/foo.md` → `/mnt/torus/mcp-data/files/notes/system/specs/foo.md` · `workspaces://universal-llm-gateway/libs/x.py` → `/mnt/torus/projects/universal-llm-gateway/libs/x.py`.

## Access preference

| Prefer | When |
|---|---|
| IDE / shell file tools (`Read`, `Grep`, `Write`, …) | Bulk or targeted reads/writes of known paths on this host — fewer MCP round-trips |
| MCP `fs` (`md_list`, `md_read`, `md_*` writes, Share-URI ops) | Markdown section listing, navigation, and section edits; cross-resident or when Share URI semantics matter |

## Citation

Reports, closeouts, assertions, packets, and handoffs reference `cortex://…` / `workspaces://…` — ¬ bake `/mnt/torus/…` into durable text. Local paths are an access affordance, not the public address.

